// anthropic:provider — a concrete LLM provider implementing `llm:inference`.
//
// The other side of the swap point, for Anthropic's Messages API. `llm:inference`
// defines the vendor-agnostic shape of a chat call; this implements it by POSTing
// to `/v1/messages`. Which provider a deployment links is a wasi:config choice;
// nothing upstream (the agent, the driver) knows Anthropic was chosen.
//
// Why a SEPARATE component from openai-provider rather than a config flag on it:
// the wire contracts genuinely differ. Anthropic authenticates with `x-api-key`
// and an `anthropic-version` header, not a bearer token; it carries the system
// prompt as a top-level field rather than a message; its response is a list of
// content blocks, not choices; it has no `seed`; and `max_tokens` is required,
// not optional. A single component straddling both would be a runtime switch
// over two codecs, which is two components wearing one name.
//
// Config (wasi:config/store):
//   anthropic:base-url    API base, default "https://api.anthropic.com"
//   anthropic:model       default model, e.g. "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001"
//   anthropic:version     API version header, default "2023-06-01"
//   anthropic:max-tokens  cap when the caller sets none, default "4096"
//
// The KEY is a secret, granted by reference and read through comp:secrets/reader
// under `anthropic-api-key` (ADR-0010, ADR-0051) — never config.
//
// NO EMBEDDINGS. Anthropic has no embeddings endpoint (they point at a separate
// vendor), so `embed` returns invalid-request rather than pretending. A
// deployment that needs retrieval links a dedicated embedding provider for that
// one interface.
package anthropic:provider@0.1.0;

world anthropic-provider {
    export llm:inference/inference@0.1.0;
    import wasi:http/outgoing-handler@0.2.0;
    import wasi:config/store@0.2.0-rc.1;
    import comp:secrets/reader@0.1.0;
}
